ACE: Not bad. Loops can get dizzying.
Tyrone: You can say that again. I was worried it would never stop.
ACE: Behind the scenes, your "while" loop checked the condition first. As long as it stayed true, it kept repeating the block.
ACE: But because you remembered to update the variable inside, the condition eventually became false, and the loop broke.
Tyrone: So if I forgot to update it, it would just run forever?
ACE: Exactly! An infinite loop. Good thing you avoided it.
Tyrone: I feel like I barely survived that one.
